            "Natural selection",
            "Mutualism",
            "Commensalism"
          ],
          "correctAnswer": 0
        },
        {
          "question": "Two tall trees growing right next to each other are fighting to capture the same limited sunlight. What kind of interaction is this?",
          "options": [
            "Competition (-/-)",
            "Parasitism (+/-)",
            "Commensalism (+/0)"
          ],
          "correctAnswer": 0
        },
        {
          "question": "A remora fish travels attached to a shark to eat leftover food scraps. The shark is completely unaffected and does not notice. What code and name represent this interaction?",
          "options": [
            "(+/0) Commensalism",
            "(+/+) Mutualism",
            "(+/-) Predation"
          ],
          "correctAnswer": 0
        },
        {
          "question": "A tapeworm lives inside a cat's digestive system, absorbing its nutrients and weakening the animal. This relationship is:",
          "options": [
            "Parasitism (+/-)",
